
# Frequently Asked Questions

## What is Document360?

Document360 is a knowledge base platform used to create, organize, manage, and publish documentation.

## What is a knowledge base?

A knowledge base is a centralized collection of information that helps users find answers, guides, and troubleshooting instructions.

## What is an article?

An article is an individual documentation page that contains information about a particular topic.

## What is a category?

A category is used to group related articles and organize documentation.

## Can I edit a published article?

Yes. You can edit an existing article, save the changes, and publish the updated version.

## What is website crawling?

Website crawling collects content from specified website URLs so that it can be used as a chatbot knowledge source.

## What is a chatbot?

A chatbot helps users find information and answers based on its configured knowledge sources.

## What is GitHub integration?

GitHub integration allows Markdown documentation stored in a GitHub repository to be synchronized with Document360.

## Why might GitHub content not appear in Document360?

Possible reasons include an incomplete GitHub connection, repository access restrictions, an empty repository, unsupported file content, or synchronization issues.

## What should I do if an article does not appear?

Check the category, synchronization status, repository permissions, and whether the Markdown file has been committed and pushed.
